# &#x20;Domus Smart Control

### An ESP32-Based Smart Home Automation System

Domus Smart Control is an IoT-based home automation project built around the ESP32 microcontroller. It aims to improve home comfort, security and accessibility through connected devices, automated actions and remote control via a web interface.

The system combines embedded electronics, wireless communication and web technologies to create an interactive smart home environment.

## &#x20;Features

- **RFID Access Control:** Identification and access management using RFID cards.
- **Automatic Door Control:** Servo motor-based door opening and closing.
- **Smart Lighting:** RGB LED control with manual and automatic operating modes.
- **Environmental Sensing:** Sensor-based monitoring of the surrounding environment.
- **Wireless Communication:** ESP32 Wi-Fi connectivity.
- **Web Interface:** Remote interaction with the smart home system through a browser.

## Technologies & Components

### Hardware

- ESP32 DevKit V1
- RFID-RC522 module
- Servo motors
- RGB LED
- LDR light sensor
- Ultrasonic sensor

### Software

- Arduino IDE
- C/C++
- ESP32 Arduino Core
- HTML / CSS / JavaScript
- Wi-Fi communication

## System Architecture

The ESP32 acts as the central controller of the system.

It receives information from connected sensors and modules, processes the data and controls the corresponding actuators.

The web interface provides a user-friendly way to interact with the system through Wi-Fi.

