## &#x20;Installation & Setup

1. Install the Arduino IDE.
2. Configure the ESP32 board support package.
3. Connect the ESP32 to your computer.
4. Install the required libraries.
5. Open the project source code.
6. Configure your Wi-Fi settings.
7. Upload the firmware to the ESP32.
8. Connect to the ESP32 network and access the web interface.

**Note:** Hardware connections, library dependencies and network configuration must match the source code and actual prototype.

